findings.body:
**The post-merge rename can't work, and every open PR ends up with two status labels.**

The merge pushes to `main`, and `on: push: branches: [main]` starts a recompute over every open PR. The merged PR's own `closed` event (`pull_request_target`, which runs from the base branch) does the same. Both runs use the merged file, so they have the new names. Before either run labels any PR, it creates every name in `LABELS`:

```js
for (const [name, [color, description]] of Object.entries(LABELS)) {
  try {
    await github.rest.issues.createLabel({ owner, repo, name, color, description });
  } catch (e) {
    if (e.status !== 422) throw e;
  }
}
```

So `draft`, `conflicts`, …, `ready` exist within seconds of the merge. Label names are unique within a repo, so the planned `gh label edit "pr/$n" --name "$n"` fails with 422 `already_exists` for each name.

The same run then adds the new label to every open PR. Its removal loop (L200-L208) only goes through `Object.keys(LABELS)`, which no longer includes any `pr/` name. Nothing removes the old `pr/ready`, `pr/ci-pending` and so on, so a PR can show `pr/ready` and `ci-failing` at once. Those are the duplicates the PR description means to avoid.

Renaming before the merge doesn't help either, as the description notes.

**Options:**
- Do the rename inside the workflow, before anything is created. A rename keeps the label on every PR that has it. The suggestion below lets 404 (already renamed, or a concurrent run won) and 422 (both names exist) fall through to `createLabel`, so no state makes every later run fail. Delete the shim once no `pr/*` label is left.
- With no code change: after the merge, run `gh label delete "pr/$n" --yes` instead of `edit`. You lose only the label timeline history.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/6b1bbc46414bd38c8a7dca6f9d9c3de8e01eec09/.github/workflows/pr-status.yml#L185-L191

findings.suggestion:
for (const [name, [color, description]] of Object.entries(LABELS)) {
  try {
    // One-off move off the `pr/` prefix, run before any label is created: a rename keeps
    // the label on every PR it is on. Delete once no `pr/*` label is left.
    await github.rest.issues.updateLabel({ owner, repo, name: `pr/${name}`, new_name: name });
    continue;
  } catch (e) {
    if (e.status !== 404 && e.status !== 422) throw e;
  }
  try {
    await github.rest.issues.createLabel({ owner, repo, name, color, description });
  } catch (e) {
    if (e.status !== 422) throw e;
  }
}
